# Web app rules (`apps/web`, `packages/*`)

## Stack constraints

- **Vanilla TypeScript only.** No React/Vue/JSX/virtual DOM, no UI
  frameworks, no state libraries. Components are functions returning
  `HTMLElement` in `src/ui/`. Tiny hand-rolled pub/sub for state.
- Features live in `src/features/<zone>/`; router/shell in `src/app/`;
  Supabase client and helpers in `src/lib/`.
- Dependencies require strong justification — prefer zero.

## Sky Design System

- Tokens come ONLY from `@poxy/tokens` (`tokens.json` is the machine source;
  `css/variables.css` its generated projection). **Zero hardcoded hex** in
  `apps/web` outside the tokens package. Locked values: Sky-500 `#60C2E0`,
  ink `#1C1C1E`, paper `#F0F0F1`.
- Dual environment via `data-env="gallery|vault"` switching semantic
  variables — never fork components per environment.
- Rarity colors only in gem SVGs and `RarityBadge`/figure-card gems.
- Type roles: UI = SF Pro/Inter; display numbers = Space Grotesk; hashes,
  seeds and mint numbers = JetBrains Mono. Syne only in the landing hero.
- Motion: 200ms micro / 320ms panel / 600–900ms ritual-only, easing
  `cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1)`. Always honor `prefers-reduced-motion`
  (ritual → 150ms crossfade).

## Mobile & accessibility

- Mobile-first; verify at **390px**: no horizontal scroll, touch targets
  ≥44px, contrast AA for text tokens, focus-visible ring in Sky-500.

## Copy

- Brand voice (docs/10-BRAND.md): sentence case, no exclamation marks, no
  hype adjectives, no em-dashes in user-facing copy. Errors = fact + fix.
- Odds are ALWAYS visible before purchase. Never hide or delay them.

## Data discipline

- All value mutations go through edge functions — the client never writes
  wallets, mints, openings, listings directly.
- Render user content as `textContent`, never `innerHTML` (XSS). Every
  `innerHTML` use must be justified against untrusted input.
- Rive is deferred: build `data-rive-slot` placeholders (star gem), do not
  add the Rive runtime to the app until the dedicated post-beta session.
